[{:db/id "q-8462/selection/7121f411ab946dc9ce849a45d309124b7af86feb950f0c3ae3801e6d6d5f545c" :answer/id #uuid "0b1c8e04-fe78-5854-878f-eb039f649e8b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8462/selection/158378e17021eac10134da6b83924ebc0fafedadd9fd334cafb885ba71be156b" :answer/id #uuid "70b0a532-9631-521c-b6e5-9bee37cd26fb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A rotation of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians counterclockwise about the origin." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8462/selection/48da0b2e9bdbcdebc6b95c2b61c8be2a42b06e50a667ac2c5aea1433aad9828a" :answer/id #uuid "00cace13-12a2-540e-b99d-d9f1a1b8c4da" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A rotation of $\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ radians clockwise about the origin." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8462/selection/e61483fe328d5a1bd08dc326fa81e15c7ff4c8baad77057a9a448adba4977c78" :answer/id #uuid "82005ba9-863a-5174-994e-8c3e08e414e0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A rotation of $\\frac{3\\pi }{4}$ radians clockwise about the origin." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8462/selection/0685937c9b1e769201847cae592f7c6a812dee3109951d43e7f5c9ad554e5d15" :answer/id #uuid "c04d064d-bf85-5b49-b89e-0159debae0fe" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians clockwise about the origin." :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-8462/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74b9d120-8cc0-55e1-9b99-e9038213d12a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-8462/selection/0685937c9b1e769201847cae592f7c6a812dee3109951d43e7f5c9ad554e5d15" :answer-field/choices ["q-8462/selection/7121f411ab946dc9ce849a45d309124b7af86feb950f0c3ae3801e6d6d5f545c" "q-8462/selection/158378e17021eac10134da6b83924ebc0fafedadd9fd334cafb885ba71be156b" "q-8462/selection/48da0b2e9bdbcdebc6b95c2b61c8be2a42b06e50a667ac2c5aea1433aad9828a" "q-8462/selection/e61483fe328d5a1bd08dc326fa81e15c7ff4c8baad77057a9a448adba4977c78" "q-8462/selection/0685937c9b1e769201847cae592f7c6a812dee3109951d43e7f5c9ad554e5d15"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-8462" :question/id #uuid "29bbf036-1652-5f64-8437-aab9ecbcce39" :question/math-academy-id "q-8462" :question/problem "What is the geometrical interpretation of the transformation represented by the matrix $A$ given below? \n\n \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The rotation matrix ${R}_{\\theta }$ represents a rotation of angle $\\theta $ counterclockwise about the origin and is given by\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nComparing $A$ with the rotation matrix, we have \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta <0$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta >0$ we must have $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le 2\\pi .$ \n\nDividing the first equation by the second gives\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =-1.\n$$\n\nThe principal value $\\theta $ is\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{4},\n$$\n\nTherefore, $A$ represents a rotation of $\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ radians *clockwise* about the origin." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-8462/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "bea036e3-19cd-572b-a6cb-2fa466c2a399"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-8462"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275762/field-1/6b95511de4de11a307ef0b59561676b4ba5acdacebc5c441c2ab3b04050b282b" :answer/id #uuid "c7015b36-5afc-55b6-869f-c935692d23a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275762/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c" :answer/id #uuid "cd0caff6-8f48-5be7-9085-d609c3d4599f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275762/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0b591c7-a748-56fa-a41f-0b676f1b2f46" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275762/field-1/6b95511de4de11a307ef0b59561676b4ba5acdacebc5c441c2ab3b04050b282b" :answer-field/choices ["q-275762/field-1/6b95511de4de11a307ef0b59561676b4ba5acdacebc5c441c2ab3b04050b282b" "q-275762/field-1/af5580a233ee3709064249d6732fc822dfb93f38caf90c025deb51b127e90b2c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275762/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "8f547cfe-3beb-500b-9ff9-84833f886e86" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275762/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "5b5ae671-e78b-502c-a95a-224fc95282b1" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275762/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-275762/field-2/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275762" :question/id #uuid "820b5d3a-ac10-512c-a999-f8c05a95082f" :question/math-academy-id "q-275762" :question/problem "The vector $v=⟨-2,-2⟩$ is rotated ${45}^{∘}$ **clockwise** about the origin. Find the image of $v$ under this rotation.\n\n${v}^{′}=⟨$\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "A rotation of ${45}^{∘}$ *clockwise* about the origin is represented by the matrix \n\n$$\n{R}_{(-{45}^{∘})}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{45}^{∘}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{45}^{∘}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{45}^{∘}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{45}^{∘})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image ${v}^{′}$ under the action of the matrix ${R}_{(-{45}^{∘})}$, we compute the matrix product, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{′} & ={R}_{(-{45}^{∘})}\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image is ${v}^{′}=⟨-2\\sqrt{2},0⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275762/field-1" "q-275762/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "add52a4e-fff5-5cf6-8fe9-85a44063e2a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275762"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-279364/field-1/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer/id #uuid "d47c04a9-561f-5a0e-9ec2-ed3c493396cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279364/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "2249e823-78df-55d1-9bbf-6f161f32c319" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279364/field-1/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63" :answer-field/choices ["q-279364/field-1/f00d8b7a5eeed0dcaa02b7f16c350647a90a461726a760f9ecdf0379dbf8fa63"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279364/field-2/df4ef3a75f6d71027299791921d9536d50890079e16123ff435f8ed8ac6150b0" :answer/id #uuid "cff6832f-08f3-5294-a0bf-4fc631584b80" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-279364/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "81a98fac-9a0c-5216-9d36-b078269dc964" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-279364/field-2/df4ef3a75f6d71027299791921d9536d50890079e16123ff435f8ed8ac6150b0" :answer-field/choices ["q-279364/field-2/df4ef3a75f6d71027299791921d9536d50890079e16123ff435f8ed8ac6150b0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-279364" :question/id #uuid "5988de2b-cef4-5593-b032-d7b4902c83df" :question/math-academy-id "q-279364" :question/problem "The vector $v=⟨-4,-2⟩$ is rotated ${225}^{∘}$ **clockwise** about the origin. Find the image of $v$ under this rotation.\n\n${v}^{′}=⟨$\n{{field-1}}, \n{{field-2}}\n$⟩$" :question/worked-solution "A rotation of ${225}^{∘}$ *clockwise* about the origin is represented by the matrix \n\n$$\n{R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(-{225}^{∘}) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(-{225}^{∘})\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image ${v}^{′}$ under the action of the matrix ${R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}$, we compute the matrix product, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}^{′} & ={R}_{(-{225}^{∘})}\\cdot v \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2} & -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3\\sqrt{2} \\\\ -\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the image is ${v}^{′}=⟨3\\sqrt{2},-\\sqrt{2}⟩.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-279364/field-1" "q-279364/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "add52a4e-fff5-5cf6-8fe9-85a44063e2a8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-279364"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
